<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39690" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pūtĕo</span></b> ,
		ēre (no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i> or <i>sup.</i>),
				2, v. n.
			Sanscr. root pu-, to stink; cf. pus; Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦον</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To stink</i> (cf. putesco), Cic. Fragm. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 545, 16</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">putet aper,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 2, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">putere diurno mero,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ep. 1, 19, 11</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Pers. 3, 73</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To be rotten</i>, <i>putrid</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 1, 2, 67</span></i> (al.
			putrent).—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pū-tens</span></b> , entis, P.
			a., <i>stinking</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Aldh. Laud. Virg. 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Scrib.
				Comp. 186</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
